# ERP UI Rules

## Component usage

1. Always reuse existing components from `src/components/ui` and `src/components/shared`.
2. ECME components are the primary UI components.
3. Never install another UI library without explicit approval.
4. Never recreate an existing ECME component (Button, Card, Input, Dialog, Table, Select, etc.).
5. Do not modify ECME primitives in `src/components/ui` unless fixing a bug or an approved design-system change.
6. Keep UI consistent across all modules.

## Before implementing a page

1. Inspect `src/components/ui` and `src/components/shared`.
2. Prefer composing existing pieces over creating new ones.
3. Create a new shared component only when no existing component can satisfy the requirement.
4. Put domain-specific components under `src/modules/<module>/components`.

## Page structure

```text
Page → PageHeader → Filters/Actions → Summary → Main Content
```

## Preferred building blocks

- Tables: `DataTable` (`src/components/shared/DataTable.tsx`)
- Forms: `Form`, `FormItem`, `FormContainer`, `Input`, `Select`, `DatePicker`, `Checkbox`, `Radio`, `Dialog`
- Cards/stats: `Card`, `AdaptiveCard`, `GrowShrinkValue`, `AbbreviateNumber`
- Status: `Tag`, `StatusBadge`, `Badge`
- Charts: `Chart`
- Layout chrome: existing `layouts` + `template` — do not rebuild the shell

## Styling

- Follow existing ECME Tailwind theme and tokens.
- Do not introduce arbitrary one-off color systems.
- Do not introduce another design system.
